comments.body:
🤖 NCCL development commit `7aea0aa7` provides a sharp A/B for this reproducer but is not a usable fix.

With an exclusively mapped NCCL 2.31.0 runtime:
- eager RMA init off reproduces the post-lowering JaxPP execution deadlock after all known DIME links and local tasks are prewarmed/precompiled;
- `NCCL_RMA_EAGER_INIT=1` removes the deadlock and all four stages return, confirming the subset-rank RMA initialization change affects the failure;
- numerical validation then fails on stage 0 only: exact loss and passing stages 1-3, but stage-0 max gradient relative-L2 is 2051906.2991 under the unchanged 0.002 per-leaf gate.

The direct ragged collective and standalone four-stage VJP both pass exactly with the same library, so the corruption requires the full JaxPP stage-0 backward transfer/execution interaction. No NVIDIA issue was filed. The jobs are terminal and no resources remain live.
